<div><strong><em>Copula</em></strong></div>
<div class="row grammar-cell">
    <div>Something is something else</div>
    <div>noun-<strong>(i)eyo</strong></div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">우리 집사람<span class="grammar-verbs-highlight">이에요</span></div>
    <div>uri chipsaram-ieyo</div>
    <div>our wife-is</div>
    <div>(This person) is my wife</div>
    <div>noun-<strong>(i)seyo</strong> (with respect)</div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">선생님<span class="grammar-verbs-highlight">이세요</span>?</div>
    <div>sŏnsaengnim-iseyo?</div>
    <div>teacher to be?</div>
    <div>Are you the teacher?</div>
    <div>noun-<strong>anieyo</strong> (negative)</div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">학과가 <span class="grammar-verbs-highlight">아니에요</span></div>
    <div>hakkwa-ga anieyo</div>
    <div>department-[subject] is not</div>
    <div>(This) is not the department</div>
    <div>noun-<strong>ŏttaeyo</strong> (statement: is how?)</div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">사업은 <span class="grammar-verbs-highlight">어때요</span>?</div>
    <div>saŏb-ŭn ŏttaeyo?</div>
    <div>business-[topic] is how?</div>
    <div>How is business?</div>
    <div>noun-<strong>kŭraeyo</strong> (statement: is like that, really?, it is so)</div>
    <div>noun-<strong>ŏdieyo</strong> (statement: where is it?)</div>
    <div>noun-<strong>ŏdi issŏyo</strong> (statement: where is it?)</div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">학교가 거기 <span class="grammar-verbs-highlight">있어요</span></div>
    <div>hakkyo-ga kŏgi issŏyo</div>
    <div>school-[subject] over there there is</div>
    <div>The school is over there</div>
    <div>noun-<strong>(i)ya</strong> (plain style)</div>
</div>
<div><strong><em>Relative</em></strong></div>
<div class="row grammar-cell">
    <div>Subordinate clause that modifies a noun phrase</div>
    <div>object<em>(referent)</em> verb-<strong>n</strong>(completed plain verb)<em>(relative pronoun)</em> + subject<em>(antecedent)</em></div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">우유를 <span class="grammar-verbs-highlight">마신</span> 고양이</div>
    <div>uyurŭl mashin goyangi</div>
    <div>The cat that/who drank the milk</div>
</div>
<div><strong><em>Conditional</em></strong></div>
<div class="row grammar-cell">
    <div>Subordinate clause that expresses a requirement</div>
    <div>verb-<strong>(ŭ)myŏn</strong></div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">우체국 쪽으로 가<span class="grammar-verbs-highlight">면</span> 은행이 있어요</div>
    <div>uch'eguk cchog-ŭro ka-myŏn ŭnhaeng-i issŏyo</div>
    <div>post office side-towards go-if bank-[subject] there is</div>
    <div>If you go in the direction of the post office, there is a bank</div>
</div>
